hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18082","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Ziyad ibn Labid, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned something, he said: And that at the time of the departure of knowledge. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, knowledge departs while we recite the Quran and teach it to our sons, and our sons shall teach it to their sons until the Day of Resurrection. He said: May your mother bereave you, O son of Umm Labid, I used to see you among the most understanding men in Madinah. Are not these Jews and Christians reciting the Torah and the Gospel, yet they benefit nothing from what is in them."
"18083","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrating from Ibn Labid al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the time of the departure of knowledge. Shubah said, or he said: This is the time of the cessation of knowledge. Then I said: And how, while among us is the Book of Allah, we teach it to our sons, and our sons shall teach it to their sons. He said: May your mother bereave you, Ibn Labid, I counted you only among the most intelligent of the people of Madinah. Are not the Jews and the Christians among them the Book of Allah Almighty. Shubah said, or he said: Are not the Jews and the Christians among them the Torah and the Gospel, then they benefited nothing from it. Or he said: Are not the Jews and the Christians, or the People of the Book, Shubah says that, among them the Book of Allah Almighty."
